  \end{align*}
 for some interval $I \subseteq (N/2,N']$, with $B_i$ given in~\eqref{eq:B1def} and~\eqref{eq:B2def}. 

Observe that for both $B_1$ and $B_2$, we have $N^{1/3}/2\leq p_1p_2\leq N^{2/3}$. Thus, letting $n_1=p_1p_2$ and $n_2=p_3$, dyadically splitting the variables, and removing the cross-condition $n_1n_2\in I$ by~\eqref{eq:removcross}, we obtain an admissible type II sum. 

