	Since $\chi$ has modulus at most $P$, the character $\chi \psi $ (of modulus $\leq PQ$) is never principal. Let $\chi\psi$ have modulus $s$ and let it be induced by a character $\psi'$ of modulus $1<s'\leq s$. Applying M\"obius inversion and then the P\'olya--Vinogradov inequality, we get
 \begin{align*}
