    since $c_d(n)=\mu(d)$ for $(d,n)=1$. Thus, for $(n,\widetilde{r})=1$, we get
    \begin{align*}
        \Lambda_{R,1}(n)-\frac{\widetilde{r}}{\varphi(\widetilde{r})}\Lambda_{R,\widetilde{r}}(n)&= \sum_{(q,\widetilde{r})=1} \frac{\mu(q)c_{q}(n)}{\varphi(q)}\left(\sum_{d\mid \widetilde{r}} \frac{\mu(d)^2}{\varphi(d)}G\left(\frac{\log dq}{\log R}\right)- \frac{\widetilde{r}}{\varphi(\widetilde{r})} G\left(\frac{\log \widetilde{r}q}{\log R}\right)\right)\\
